Date: Sun, 2 Aug 2026 21:01:52 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] gallery: zoom and pan the picture being viewed

Snapshot shows a saved picture scaled to fit and stops there, which throws
away most of what the camera recorded: the rear sensor writes 4032x3024 and
the screen shows about a tenth of those pixels. Checking whether a shot came
out sharp - the one thing a viewer is for right after taking it - could only
be done by leaving the app.

Replace the GtkPicture the gallery shows a photograph in with a widget that
draws the same paintable through a zoom factor and an offset, driven by a
pinch, a scroll wheel or a double tap, and dragged around once magnified.
The offset is clamped so the picture always covers the window: a drag cannot
push it off-screen and leave nothing to drag back.

The drag claims the gesture only while there is more picture than window, so
at fit size the gallery's own swipe still pages through the pictures, and
paging away resets the view rather than returning to a picture magnified and
half off-centre from last time.
